<!-- HTML Link Ke Zariye -->
<script>
  // Page load hone par URL se parameters nikalna
  window.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    // 1. Current URL ke query parameters GET karein
    const urlParams = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);

    // 2. Specific Key ka value read karein
    const name = urlParams.get('name');   // "Rahul"
    const phone = urlParams.get('phone'); // "9876543210"

    console.log("Name:", name);
    console.log("Phone:", phone);

    // 3. (Optional) Auto-fill Input Fields (Aapke Form Me Set Karne Ke Liye)
    if (name) {
      document.getElementById('fullName').value = name;
    }
    if (phone) {
      document.getElementById('phoneNumber').value = phone;
    }
  });
</script>

//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

<!-- HTML Link Ke Zariye -->
<a href="contact.html?name=Rahul&phone=9876543210">Contact Rahul</a>

<script>
  // JavaScript Ke Zariye Page Open Ya Redirect Karte Waqt:
  function goToPage() {
    const name = "Rahul";
    const phone = "9876543210";
    
    // URL Encoding use karein taaki spaces/special characters handle ho sakein
    window.location.href = `contact.html?name=${encodeURIComponent(name)}&phone=${encodeURIComponent(phone)}`;
  }
</script>

//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////


Key Points (Dhyan Rakhne Yogy Baatein):
encodeURIComponent(): Jab aap URL me spaces ya special characters (&, =, ?) bhej rahe hon, toh use hamesha encodeURIComponent('value') se pass karein.

Security: URL parameters sabhi ko visible hote hain. Isme sensitive data jaise Password ya Card details kabhi mat bhejein.
